{
  "case_id": "2007-07-214",
  "document_hash": "15e621d3f755137ef044819e41c153616da5dd56c52aaccc645d840fb3077e8f",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-07-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15e621d3f755137ef044819e41c153616da5dd56c52aaccc645d840fb3077e8f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15e621d3f755-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: What about the certificates of conformance with specifications of? I believe they were the Navy's specifications and Allison submitted to someone those certificates of conformance."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Olson",
      "case_id": "2007-07-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15e621d3f755137ef044819e41c153616da5dd56c52aaccc645d840fb3077e8f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15e621d3f755-0000-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There is no evidence in this case that false or fraudulent claims were submitted to the United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2007-07-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15e621d3f755137ef044819e41c153616da5dd56c52aaccc645d840fb3077e8f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15e621d3f755-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Did the Navy have the right to audit the subcontractor's books?\nMR. OLSON: It's my understanding -- I'm not 100 percent sure of that, Justice Kennedy, but it's my understanding that the government did have the right to follow the process all the way through. There's no evidence that they did so."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (government)",
      "case_id": "2007-07-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15e621d3f755137ef044819e41c153616da5dd56c52aaccc645d840fb3077e8f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15e621d3f755-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the government says as long as the project involved Federal money, as long as the project used Federal funds, as long as the project might endanger the Federal fisc, as long as the program is financed in part by Federal money, there would be liability under this statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2007-07-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15e621d3f755137ef044819e41c153616da5dd56c52aaccc645d840fb3077e8f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15e621d3f755-0001-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF MALCOLM L. STEWART, ON BEHALF OF THE UNITED STATES, AS AMICUS CURIAE, SUPPORTING THE RESPONDENTS MR. STEWART: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: I'd like to begin with the same point that Mr. Olson began with, namely, does the False Claims Act -- is the False Claims Act directed solely at schemes to defraud the government or does it encompass schemes to defraud people who receive Federal money?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2007-07-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15e621d3f755137ef044819e41c153616da5dd56c52aaccc645d840fb3077e8f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15e621d3f755-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What you are saying is covered, I take it -- and this is -- I want to know how this has worked out -- what is covered is -- imagine government grant programs. And suppose there are vast numbers of grant programs now that go to all kinds of entities throughout the country, and a large portion of which are just grants. They're paid and the government is not going to get a penny back."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-07-214",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "15e621d3f755137ef044819e41c153616da5dd56c52aaccc645d840fb3077e8f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15e621d3f755-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Before -- before you finish, the major objection is the one that Justice Breyer just voiced, that your position is vastly overbroad and every time there's government money there will be -- one of these qui tam people can come in. What are the limiting principles that you say attach to this statute?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stewart",
      "case_id": "2007-07-214",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "15e621d3f755137ef044819e41c153616da5dd56c52aaccc645d840fb3077e8f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15e621d3f755-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There are two principal limiting principles. The first is that the bill has to be submitted to the contractor or grantee in his capacity as such. That is, there has to be a nexus between the provision of Federal funds and the request that's made. So if a subcontractor defrauds Boeing on work that Boeing is doing for a private airline, there's no FCA violation. Even though Boeing literally is a government contractor, it's not being defrauded in its capacity as such."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-07-214",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "15e621d3f755137ef044819e41c153616da5dd56c52aaccc645d840fb3077e8f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15e621d3f755-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But if injuring the Federal Government would -- it would suffice to injure the Federal Government that the schools are shoddy and the roofs are leaking? That would be enough?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-07-214",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "15e621d3f755137ef044819e41c153616da5dd56c52aaccc645d840fb3077e8f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15e621d3f755-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Whose certificate is it? Is it the contractor's certificate that everything that the subs have done or the certificate of conformance that Allison provided, that SOFCO provided?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2007-07-214",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "15e621d3f755137ef044819e41c153616da5dd56c52aaccc645d840fb3077e8f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15e621d3f755-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What about the statement that Mr. Olson quoted during his argument, when counsel for plaintiffs said to the jury: You haven't seen anything that was submitted to the Navy and you're not going to see anything that was submitted to the Navy?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-07-214",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "15e621d3f755137ef044819e41c153616da5dd56c52aaccc645d840fb3077e8f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15e621d3f755-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So your argument -- your understanding of the scope of the statute is exactly the same if the words \"by the government\" were replaced by \"with Federal funds\"? You think those are -- you think the statute is exactly the same if it said \"with Federal funds\" instead of \"by the government\"?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-07-214",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "15e621d3f755137ef044819e41c153616da5dd56c52aaccc645d840fb3077e8f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15e621d3f755-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But that was only the contract. You didn't show that in fact that had happened, that the certificates of conformance actually were shown to a naval officer?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Olson",
      "case_id": "2007-07-214",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "15e621d3f755137ef044819e41c153616da5dd56c52aaccc645d840fb3077e8f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15e621d3f755-0002-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Let me address the -- what seems to be a controversy as to what was submitted to the Navy. In the first place, the invoices were not submitted to the Navy. We know that. That's the provision that I quoted before."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2007-07-214",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "15e621d3f755137ef044819e41c153616da5dd56c52aaccc645d840fb3077e8f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15e621d3f755-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Let me ask you this question: Suppose they had submitted the qualification certificate, but not a claim? Would they have had a case, under your view?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2007-07-214",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "15e621d3f755137ef044819e41c153616da5dd56c52aaccc645d840fb3077e8f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15e621d3f755-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: What I am really asking is: Do they still need a claim?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Olson",
      "case_id": "2007-07-214",
      "confidence": 0.6,
      "document_hash": "15e621d3f755137ef044819e41c153616da5dd56c52aaccc645d840fb3077e8f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15e621d3f755-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "MR. OLSON: I -- they -- there has to be --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2007-07-214",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "15e621d3f755137ef044819e41c153616da5dd56c52aaccc645d840fb3077e8f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15e621d3f755-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The government said in its brief if the government is the ultimate source of the funds."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-07-214",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "15e621d3f755137ef044819e41c153616da5dd56c52aaccc645d840fb3077e8f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15e621d3f755-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, Mr. Olson. The case is submitted."
    },
